    "statement": "Every pinned description/input/output/note paragraph and sample preserved. Exact renderer reproduction verified; only explicitly public-attested exponent replacements for 440B. No omitted essential images, interactions or special-checker dependency.",
    "derivation": "Unmoved cars must constitute a consecutive interval of values in increasing position order: a moved car can only be placed at an endpoint, never between unmoved cars. Conversely any such interval can be kept while smaller and larger cars move to the corresponding endpoints. Thus minimum moves = n minus longest consecutive-value increasing-position interval. Independently reverse-BFS checked all 46233 permutations of sizes 1 through 8.",
